<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>In spirit hear His trumpet voice;</l><l>We must be turned to see His choice—</l><l>The seven lampstands golden fair;</l><l>The Son of Man is walking there.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>The great high priestly robe He wears,</l><l>For every church He fully cares:</l><l>He trims the lamp, the oil supplies;</l><l>He makes them burn, flames in His eyes.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>A golden girdle on His breast—</l><l>His work is done, and from His rest</l><l>He unto all the churches pours</l><l>Himself in love, the treasure store.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>His head, His hair is white as wool—</l><l>The ancient One with youth is full.</l><l>His face is shining as the sun</l><l>To burn and lighten every one.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>Oh, when this living One we see,</l><l>We’ll fall as dead, we’ll finished be.</l><l>But then the Lord His comfort gives—</l><l>He once was dead, but now He lives.</l></lg>
<lg label="7."><l>Let every church just love Him more</l><l>His riches then He will outpour.</l><l>All other loves now lay aside;</l><l>Let’s take this Jesus, none beside.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
